# The F/P's fourth and last class node. A lash poisons two enemies, and the
# poison explodes every two seconds for five lines, harder each time.
#
# The build-up is the skill. GMS's poison builds on anything that survives an
# explosion: each helping adds 60 percentage points to the next, five deep, so a
# boss goes from 330% to 630% over six explosions and stays there. That is what
# `skill_pct_per_repeat` was built for: on a boss the helpings and the
# explosions are the same count, because it survives them all.
#
# The two caps set the damage, not the clock. GMS allows nine explosions per
# enemy and seventeen across all enemies, and the poison lasts up to twenty
# seconds, so the count runs out first and the interval only spreads the nine.
# Nine at two seconds fill eighteen of the twenty.
#
# GMS publishes no interval: the client, the wiki and namu all say only
# "periodically", and the one unused number in its common block is the three
# crystals a map can hold, not a beat. Two seconds is ours, and it is limited,
# not arbitrary: above 20/9 of a second the nine-explosion cap could never be
# reached on a boss, which is exactly where GMS meant it to apply.
#
# GMS's final explosion ("all poison is removed, followed by an additional
# explosion") is not a tick. It lands with the ninth, at the top of the ramp;
# that is `final_repeat_strike`.
#
# The crystal is dropped, and the spreading with it. Both are how GMS moves the
# poison off a dead mob, and the total is capped either way: two enemies
# exploding nine times each is eighteen against GMS's seventeen. What is lost is
# that a newly infected mob starts its ramp again, so a crowd is worth a bit
# more here than in GMS. On a boss, where this skill matters, there is nothing
# to spread to.
#
# This poison is not a burn. GMS says plainly it doesn't trigger Elemental
# Drain, so it is a pulse, not a `dot`, and DoT Punisher's orb count and Fervent
# Drain's final damage don't count it.
name: "Poison Chain"
description:
  "Unleash a fatal poison on a chain of enemies. Poisoned enemies "
  "periodically release clouds of additional poison, damaging both "
  "themselves and other nearby enemies. Even if they survive the initial "
  "explosion, the poison effect stacks, raising the power of further "
  "explosions. Unaffected by attack reflection."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_ARCH_MAGE_V skill_order: 4 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_STAFF
base_delay_ms: 660
cooldown_seconds: 25.0
max_enemies: 2
lines: 4
base { skill_pct: 2.60 }
per_level { skill_pct: 0.10 }
buff {
  duration_seconds: 20.0
  pulse {
    label: "Poison Explosion"
    cast_interval_seconds: 2.0
    lines: 5
    max_pulses: 9
    final_repeat_strike: true
    max_repeats: 5
    skill_pct_per_repeat: 0.31
    skill_pct_per_repeat_per_level: 0.01
    base { skill_pct: 1.56 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.06 }
  }
}
